{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ADR + docs pushed for review as Gerrit change 1339 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1339), commit ef3a32e560 on d8625-adr from origin/main 9af88c3ada. NOT submitted, ticket left in_progress pending LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1.\n\nADR number: 0059 (docs/adr/0059-llm-provider-seam-and-support-tiers.md), matching the recorded file_impact. Confirmed free two ways: 'ls docs/adr/' shows 0058 as the high-water mark, and 'git log --all --diff-filter=A -- docs/adr/0059* docs/adr/0060*' returns nothing after fetching BOTH origin and gerrit (both at 9af88c3ada).\n\nAlso changed docs/llm-framework.md (provider-resolution section rewritten, tier table + Bedrock recipe added, env-var table filled in and defaults corrected). docs/env-vars.md needed NO change: it is generated and 'gen_env_registry.py --check' exits 0 both before and after, because this change adds no new env-var READ in Python.\n\nCorrections applied to the pre-existing draft:\n(a) cutover landed - new ADR section 10 records the production bot on Bedrock with the change-1329 provenance and the 8/8-Bedrock call log; the FallbackModel rejection and the 'landings stop' consequence are re-cast as live posture rather than plan.\n(b) local dev - section 10 describes rebar.toml's [llm.model_classes] selecting Bedrock and cites d2ce as the ticket that set it, with an explicit 'read d2ce's state before quoting this' hedge. d2ce was in_progress at authoring time, so the paragraph is written to be true once d2ce lands and is not asserted as already-verified.\n(c) the '--extra bedrock is required or the gate dies' premise is FALSE - now correction #1, first-class, including the reasoning error (absence of the EXTRA inferred as absence of the MODULE, 'confirmed' by reading packaging rather than executing the import). Re-measured here: pydantic-ai-slim 1.107.1's bedrock extra contributes exactly boto3>=1.42.63, and pydantic_ai.providers.bedrock imports from the base wheel.\n(d) 61d8-ff23-8ee0-4289 cited by id in three places.\n(e) nine rotted line anchors fixed - see the ticket's next comment.\n(f) 1c39 (un-gated terraform drift) and 9baf (voter_errors alarm has no alarm_actions) cited where they bear on the seam's rough edges; 4e71 cited as the closed AWS_REGION fix with the corrected botocore version 1.43.62. 66af deliberately NOT referenced and NOT linked.\n\nGates, all by exit code on the committed tree (git status --porcelain empty): make lint 0, make typecheck 0, check_config_reads.py 0, gen_env_registry.py --check 0, check_comment_hygiene.py 0, pytest -m 'not integration and not external' -n 6 => 0 (9819 passed, 42 skipped)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785808718480020001,"uuid":"8092556b-f817-4ab5-a510-b61e976e9d98"}